{#
  DETAIL-UX-ORIENT-01: RETURN TO ORIGIN partial. Emits the JS-revealed
  "back to where you came from" link WITHOUT any always-visible
  hub-link. Site orientation is handled separately (sidebar
  `content-context-archive-link`).

  Hidden by default (`d-none`) with `href="#"` placeholder. The
  anchor becomes visible and gains a real href ONLY when
  `src/js/site-ui.js` finds a valid `?returnTo=` on the current URL
  matching `data-detail-return-prefixes`. If no origin exists we do
  NOT surface a synthetic "back to hub" link — the sidebar/domain-hub
  SITE ORIENTATION link is sufficient. Return-to-origin and site
  orientation are two different semantic layers.

  Contextual label (URL contract):
    - JS reads `?returnLabel=` and, when the return context is valid,
      uses it as the anchor's textContent (length-capped + whitespace-
      normalized).
    - Otherwise the anchor keeps the SSR default label stored as
      `data-detail-return-default-label`.

  Consumers (trailing `<footer class="content-detail-origin">` region):
    - media-item.njk
    - presentation-item.njk
    - writing-post.njk

  Publications + Theses continue to use `detail-orientation.njk`
  (hub-link + return-link inside the same trailing footer) because
  their sidebar `content-context-archive-link` points at `/kynasta/`
  (topical umbrella), not the domain hub — so both the always-visible
  domain hub AND the return link must render.

  Inputs (set by caller as Nunjucks vars):
    orientationLang                — currentLang for label
    orientationReturnFallback      — canonical hub URL used for
                                     DUPLICATE-SUPPRESSION ONLY (never
                                     assigned as the anchor's href).
                                     Suppresses the return-link when
                                     `?returnTo=` would resolve to the
                                     same URL as the page's SSR
                                     orientation link (avoids
                                     rendering a duplicate).
    orientationReturnPrefixes      — pathname prefix allowlist
    orientationReturnLabel         — optional default label; falls
                                     back to "Takaisin hakutuloksiin" /
                                     "Back to results" for
                                     compatibility with legacy Find &
                                     Explore links that omit the new
                                     `returnLabel` param.
#}
{% set _returnLang = orientationLang or lang or (page.url | langFromUrl) %}
{% set _returnFallback = orientationReturnFallback or "" %}
{% set _returnPrefixes = orientationReturnPrefixes or [] %}
{% set _returnLabel = orientationReturnLabel or ("Back to results" if _returnLang == "en" else "Takaisin hakutuloksiin") %}
<a
  class="btn btn-link fw-semibold px-0 d-none"
  href="#"
  data-detail-return-link
  data-detail-return-fallback="{{ _returnFallback }}"
  data-detail-return-prefixes="{{ _returnPrefixes | join(',') }}"
  data-detail-return-default-label="{{ _returnLabel }}">
  {{ _returnLabel }}
</a>
